# Heavy directories not needed by any Docker build
detection
# ...except the few paths service images actually COPY out of it. The blanket
# exclusion meant `docker compose --build` could not build incident-api,
# code-processor, response-orchestrator, code-enrichment-worker or
# malware-triage from the repo root at all -- the build aborted with
# "/detection/profiles: not found" -- which also broke the detection-runtime-smoke
# CI job. Listed individually so detection/ stays out of the context otherwise;
# its model artifacts and datasets are large.
!detection/profiles
!detection/playbooks
!detection/scanners/semgrep/rules
!detection/models/common
!detection/models/malware-static
!detection/models/antares-1b/assets/antares-cli
!detection/models/antares-1b/assets/antares-cli/pyproject.toml
!detection/models/antares-1b/assets/antares-cli/README.md
!detection/models/antares-1b/assets/antares-cli/LICENSE
!detection/models/antares-1b/assets/antares-cli/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!detection/models/antares-1b/assets/antares-cli/src
!detection/models/code-model/pyproject.toml
!detection/models/code-model/code_model
!detection/models/code-model/inference
!detection/models/code-model/training
!detection/models/code-model/artifacts
!detection/models/host-state-model/pyproject.toml
!detection/models/host-state-model/host_state_model
!detection/models/host-state-model/inference
!detection/models/log-model/pyproject.toml
!detection/models/log-model/log_model
!detection/models/log-model/inference
!detection/models/log-model/training
!detection/models/log-model/artifacts
!detection/models/metrics-model/pyproject.toml
!detection/models/metrics-model/metrics_model
!detection/models/metrics-model/inference
!detection/models/metrics-model/training
!detection/models/metrics-model/artifacts
!detection/models/network-model/pyproject.toml
!detection/models/network-model/network_model
!detection/models/network-model/inference
!detection/models/network-model/training
!detection/models/network-model/artifacts
models
Archive
black-onyx-tools
# ...except the MCP tool implementations and their catalog. pyproject's
# `mcp` extra installs black-onyx-tools from this path, and mcp/registry.py
# reads datasets/tool_use/tools.json at runtime. Excluding the whole
# directory left the deployed image with zero platform tools.
!black-onyx-tools/pyproject.toml
!black-onyx-tools/README.md
!black-onyx-tools/src
!black-onyx-tools/datasets/tool_use/tools.json
black-onyx-tools/.venv
black-onyx-tools/build
black-onyx-tools/tests
